# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites the working
# tree to CRLF on checkout. Prettier's endOfLine default is "lf", so
# `npm run format:check` then fails on literally every file in the repository —
# which is exactly what the first CI run on windows-latest did. `eol=lf` wins
# over core.autocrlf, so this fixes it for CI and for any Windows contributor
# without either having to configure anything.
#
# No tracked text file contains a CR today, so this pins the status quo rather
# than reformatting anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary payloads, marked explicitly rather than left to Git's heuristic.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
